[CI/unit-tests    ]   |       --network string               Network mode: cloudflare, tailscale, direct
[CI/unit-tests    ]   |       --network-mode string          Network isolation mode for this agent: shared, systemd, procvis (default: BUNKERD_NETWORK_MODE, then the server's config, then shared). systemd = private network namespace (loopback only; NO outbound — image pulls fail in this mode). procvis = private /proc in the unit's mount namespace (hidepid=2 semantics; unit processes see only their own user's processes; does NOT cover SSH/exec sessions)
[CI/unit-tests    ]   |       --preset string                Safety preset for this agent: open, standard, hardened (default: BUNKERD_SAFETY_PRESET, then the server's config, then the built-in default standard (GAP-117))
[CI/unit-tests    ]   |       --server string                Server alias (required unless BUNKER_SESSION_TARGET is set; mutating commands never fall back to the shared active default)
[CI/unit-tests    ]   |       --ssh-host string              SSH host shown in the bundle (default: hostname from server config URL)
[CI/unit-tests    ]   |       --toolchains string[="full"]   Provision a build-toolchain CLASS onto the agent right after creation (SURF-009). Classes: minimal (python3 only — what an agent without the flag is), go (go + make), full (go + gcc + make + node + cargo). Bare --toolchains means full. Downloads are checksum-pinned into the agent's HOME (no root); a failed delivery is a warning, not a spawn failure. Check anytime with 'bunker toolchain-check <agent-id> --class <class>'
[CI/unit-tests    ]   |       --tools-at-spawn               Deliver the verb tools (toolsd, rg, gopls) onto the agent as part of spawn: the registry tools ride the image-spec carrier (the canonical delivered set is attached to the request when no --image-spec is given; a custom spec must BE the delivered set), toolsd is copied from a local static artifact when one exists, and every still-missing tool is pulled through its registry stage. The result is verified by re-probing the agent; a failed delivery FAILS the spawn loudly — the agent is reported as existing but NOT provisioned. Repair in place with 'bunker agent-tools <agent-id> --install'
