[CI/unit-tests    ]   |       --tools-at-spawn               Deliver the verb tools (toolsd, rg, gopls) onto the agent as part of spawn: the registry tools ride the image-spec carrier (the canonical delivered set is attached to the request when no --image-spec is given; a custom spec must BE the delivered set), toolsd is copied from a local static artifact when one exists, and every still-missing tool is pulled through its registry stage. The result is verified by re-probing the agent; a failed delivery FAILS the spawn loudly — the agent is reported as existing but NOT provisioned. Repair in place with 'bunker agent-tools <agent-id> --install'
